Why a copy and not a git submodule like the rest of vendor/: upstream's
own repository declares nested submodules (lib/gears, utils/doxydown)
with SSH URLs, so `git clone --recurse-submodules`, `make refs`, and CI's
recursive checkout would all fail for anyone without GitHub SSH keys —
for two directories nothing here uses. The one file the pin and axle
call (parts/bitbeam/pin.scad, axle.scad) is vendored as-is instead.

To update: fetch the file at a newer commit, replace Technic.scad, and
record the commit above. Its gear modules `include <lib/gears/gears.scad>`
inside their bodies; OpenSCAD warns that it cannot find that file and
carries on, which is harmless since no part here calls a gear.
